{"step_index":1999,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-03T08:34:03Z","input_tokens":3593,"cache_read_tokens":223774,"output_tokens":3531,"thinking":"Removing the specified listeners and UI elements from `AuditScorecard.js`. Replacing the existing UI section with an updated version including the \"Save Bill to Tax Ledger\" option. Adding a new listener to connect the \"Save Ledger\" button to the corresponding function.\n\n\nFocusing on the implementation of Tab 2, a comprehensive business ledger and tax engine will be constructed. This ledger will display a table of saved bills, including columns for relevant invoice details and action buttons for viewing or deleting. Summary information will be aggregated across all stored bills, presenting totals for verified bills, purchase expenditure, and claimable GST ITC. An aggregated GST ITC ledger will be created for preparing GSTR-3B, including compliance checks for missing GSTINs and reminders about the 180-day vendor payment timeline.\n\n\nConstructing the \"Normal P&L (ITR-3)\" section involves populating purchase costs from saved bills and integrating editable input fields for operating expenses.  A live tax liability summary will be generated, incorporating tax slab calculations for the new regime and evaluating Section 87A rebates. The applicability of tax audits under Section 44AB will also be checked.\n\nData management features will include exporting the consolidated tax summary in CSV/PDF and an option to clear all stored bills.  Initializing `this.savedBills` from `localStorage` within `app.js` is essential for data persistence; a default or \"add current bill\" option will provide an immediate user experience.\n\n\nThe `handleSaveBillToLedger` function within Tab 1 will save bill data to a ledger. It retrieves invoice and audit information, calculates subtotals, taxes, and a verified total.  A new bill record is then created with essential details like invoice number, date, vendor, GSTIN, and verification status.\n\nThe existing `savedBills` are checked for a duplicate before adding the new record.  The `localStorage` is updated after the bill is added.\n\n\nChecking for duplicate invoices before saving prevents data inconsistencies. Updating an existing bill record provides data integrity. Storing the bill data in local storage allows for persistence across sessions, enabling data preservation.\n\nRetrieving bill data and switching tabs when viewing existing bills provides users with a seamless experience between the ledger and the original invoice. Removing bills and clearing stored bills ensures data management functionality. Aggregating stored bills enables calculating total purchase expenditure, CGST pools, and other summary data.\n\n\nCalculating total tax pools and claimable ITC using the sums of individual tax components and verified bill amounts is necessary. Implementing GSTIN format validation and displaying warnings for invalid GSTINs and reminders for the 180-day rule addresses statutory compliance.\n\nCreating a customizable calculator allows selection between presumptive tax (ITR-4) and normal P&L (ITR-3), with editable profit rates and sales breakdowns based on mode.\n\n\nConstructing the \"Normal P&L (ITR-3)\" section, the system will calculate deemed business net profit using digital and cash sales, with an exemption noted for Sections 44AA and 44AB. If ITR-3 mode is selected, purchase costs will be populated from saved bills or can be manually edited, with other operating expenses defaulting to a preset value. Calculating net profit involves subtracting total expenses from gross sales, with a note on the requirement of maintaining financial records.\n\nCalculating live tax liability involves deducting a standard deduction from net profit, and then applying new tax regime slabs to the resulting taxable income.  Section 87A rebate is evaluated, displaying a full rebate if the taxable income is below a threshold.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"grep -n \\\"scenarioName\\\" /Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/data/sampleInvoices.js\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolSummary":"\"Check sample invoices\""}}]}
