{"step_index":2025,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-03T08:36:33Z","input_tokens":2498,"cache_read_tokens":246329,"output_tokens":16052,"thinking":"Initial focus is on constructing the \"Tax & ITR Filing\" tab, specifically designing it as an accumulative ledger and tax engine. This involves creating a table to list all stored invoice bills, which is the initial component to implement.\n\n\nThe \"Tax & ITR Filing\" tab design incorporates an invoice bill ledger with essential columns, including date, invoice number, and tax details, culminating in a verified total and action options. A summary bar provides key expenditure and tax credit totals. An aggregated GST ITC ledger will display total eligible input tax credit, categorized by CGST, SGST, and IGST, and include statutory compliance checks.\n\nThe annual business and ITR calculator will provide interactive inputs, allowing selection between presumptive (44AD) and normal P&L modes, with corresponding calculations for deemed business net profit or net profit based on provided inputs and automatically populated purchase costs from the ledger. Live tax liability summary will present tax slabs.\n\n\nEvaluating Section 87A rebate applicability and Section 44AB tax audit thresholds are necessary features. The tab's export and clear functionalities for data management must also be incorporated. Confirmed the component structure will encompass a saved bill array, the current invoice from the first tab, an audit scorecard, state data, and callback functions for data management and interaction.\n\n\nCalculated aggregated totals from saved bills, including purchase amounts, CGST, SGST, IGST pools, and total claimable ITC. Implemented a GSTIN validation check to identify and calculate tax amounts associated with invalid GSTINs. Determined the annual turnover and calculation mode from the state, defaulting values if undefined.\n\n\nDetermining the business profit calculation based on the selected mode: 44AD or normal P&L.  In 44AD mode, profits are calculated as a percentage of sales (digital and cash), whereas the normal P&L mode calculates profits from the annual turnover less total expenses. Implementing standard deduction as well.\n\n\nCalculated the income tax based on the new tax regime, applying progressive tax rates across income slabs after standard deduction. Implemented Section 87A rebate eligibility, determining and applying the rebate if applicable. Calculated the cess and the total tax payable after accounting for the rebate.\n\nDetermined the need for a Section 44AB tax audit based on the chosen calculation mode (44AD or normal P&L) and the annual turnover. The audit threshold varies based on the digital transaction percentage.\n\n\nAudit requirement is determined based on the annual turnover and digital transaction percentage, applying the appropriate threshold. A consolidated CSV export feature generates a report including a summary, detailed bill data, and ITR planning section, allowing users to download a CSV file. The clear button triggers a confirmation prompt before deleting all stored bill data.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"\"// Component: TaxAndITRTab (Tab 2: Stored Bills Tax Ledger & Accumulative Tax Engine)\\nimport { formatRupees, round2 } from \\\"../utils/auditEngine.js\\\";\\n\\n/**\\n * Renders the full business tax ledger and accumulative tax engine\\n * @param {HTMLElement} container\\n * @param {Object} props\\n */\\nexport function renderTaxAndITRTab(container, props = {}) {\\n  const { \\n    savedBills = [], \\n    currentInvoice = null,\\n    currentAudit = null,\\n    state = {}, \\n    onUpdateState,\\n    onViewBill,\\n    onDeleteBill,\\n    onClearBills,\\n    onSaveCurrentBill\\n  } = props;\\n\\n  const formatWhole = (num) => \\\"₹\\\" + Math.round(Number(num) || 0).toLocaleString(\\\"en-IN\\\");\\n  const GSTIN_REGEX = /^[0-9]{2}[A-Z]{5}[0-9]{4}[A-Z]{1}[1-9A-Z]{1}Z[0-9A-Z]{1}$/;\\n\\n  const bills = Array.isArray(savedBills) ? savedBills : [];\\n  const totalBillsCount = bills.length;\\n\\n  // A. Aggregated Stored Bills Metrics\\n  const totalPurchases = round2(bills.reduce((sum, b) => sum + (Number(b.subtotal) || 0), 0));\\n  const totalCgstPool = round2(bills.reduce((sum, b) => sum + (Number(b.cgst) || 0), 0));\\n  const totalSgstPool = round2(bills.reduce((sum, b) => sum + (Number(b.sgst) || 0), 0));\\n  const totalIgstPool = round2(bills.reduce((sum, b) => sum + (Number(b.igst) || 0), 0));\\n  const totalClaimableITC = round2(totalCgstPool + totalSgstPool + totalIgstPool);\\n  const totalVerifiedBilled = round2(bills.reduce((sum, b) => sum + (Number(b.verified_total) || 0), 0));\\n\\n  // Statutory Compliance Check\\n  const invalidGstinBills = bills.filter(b => {\\n    const g = (b.gstin || \\\"\\\").trim().toUpperCase();\\n    return !g || g === \\\"MISSING\\\" || !GSTIN_REGEX.test(g);\\n  });\\n  const hasGstinIssues = invalidGstinBills.length > 0;\\n  const invalidGstinITC = round2(invalidGstinBills.reduce((sum, b) => sum + (Number(b.total_tax) || (Number(b.cgst)||0) + (Number(b.sgst)||0) + (Number(b.igst)||0)), 0));\\n\\n  // C. Annual Business & ITR Calculator (ITR-4 / ITR-3)\\n  const annualTurnover = Math.max(0, Number(state.annualTurnover !== undefined ? sta\n<truncated 41334 bytes>","Overwrite":"true","Path":"\"/Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/components/TaxAndITRTab.js\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
